WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:04.220
The machine didn't sign the layoff, a person did.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.920
And right now, a lot of people are hiding behind the machine.

3
00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:10.260
In my own line of work, work in the police department,

4
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.280
we never booked the crowbar, we booked the guy holding it.

5
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.460
The crowbar didn't decide to go through the back door, a person did.

6
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.280
Hold on to one word for me, signature.

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.080
I'll come back to it.

8
00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.720
Now this year, more than 100,000 announced job cuts in this country

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.480
have been blamed on artificial intelligence,

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.900
Some of that is real.

11
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.180
AI is taking over real tasks.

12
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.900
But there's a name now for the rest of it, AI washing.

13
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.280
When a company cuts people to save money or because business is slow, tells everybody

14
00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:43.280
AI did it.

15
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.420
Analysts at Deutsche Bank called it AI redundancy washing.

16
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.420
Even the CEO of OpenAI said there is some AI washing going on.

17
00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.920
It's kind of like the seller who says my market made me drop my price.

18
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.720
Well, sometimes the market really did turn.

19
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.060
And sometimes the seller just needed to move.

20
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.120
Either way, the market takes the blame.

21
00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:07.220
And the decision was theirs, ultimately.

22
00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.180
Put that blame on a legal form, and it disappears.

23
00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.980
In March of 2025, New York added a checkbox to the state's layoff notice.

24
00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.980
Is this layoff because of new technology, including AI?

25
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:25.380
Well, over the next year, more than 160 companies filed layoff notices in New York,

26
00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:27.420
and not one of them checked that box.

27
00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.940
So on the press release, AI did it.

28
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.640
on the government form, nobody did it. Same company, same layoffs. AI gets the blame when it

29
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:41.380
makes the stock look smart and disappears when it might come with a bill. Then there's the scary

30
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:46.640
robot story. You hear it every day. AI is going to wake up. AI is going to come after us. AI might

31
00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.100
have feelings. Well, nobody knows if any of that's true. Not the labs, not the scientists, definitely

32
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:57.900
not me. But one of the big labs even runs a research program on whether its AI deserves

33
00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:04.380
moral consideration because they say they don't know. And that's fine. Maybe the question matters

34
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:09.860
someday, but there's a question we can answer today. Do the people losing their jobs have

35
00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:16.520
feelings? Absolutely yes. Every single one. Whether or not the machine has feelings, the people losing

36
00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:23.840
their jobs definitely do. The labs go to Washington for rules on their own products. Some people say

37
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:28.560
that's real concern. Some people say it's building a moat. Even the White House's own

38
00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.560
advisor has accused one of the labs of using fear to shape the rules. The lab denies it. It's kind

39
00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:40.180
of like a big builder asking the city for a stricter building code after the tract is already

40
00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:45.440
finished. The code might really make the home safer, but it also makes it a lot harder for the

41
00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:51.980
next small builder to get started. Both things can be true at the same time, but don't let any of it

42
00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:57.260
distract you from the main thing. The robot story, the feeling story, the rule story,

43
00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:02.620
every one of those stories puts a spotlight on the machine. And while everybody's looking at

44
00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:10.020
the machine, nobody's looking at who's holding it. AI is a hammer. A hammer doesn't decide where to

45
00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:16.820
swing. Somebody aims it. And right now it's being aimed by the people at the top, at people on the

46
00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:23.040
ground floor. Now back to that word signature, every layoff has a signature on it. A real person,

47
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:29.120
a real name signs it. So that's the next piece of the transition moonshot that I want to build.

48
00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:35.540
If a company tells Wall Street how much AI saved them, they could tell Main Street who it costs.

49
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:43.400
Same number, same day, sign. The machine didn't sign the layoff. So let's stop letting the people

50
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.660
who did hide behind it.

51
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.400
Now tell me in the comments,

52
00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:51.060
have you been told AI took your job or a friend's job?

53
00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.100
Do you believe it?

54
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:54.660
I'm building this plan right here on the show,

55
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:56.400
one piece at a time.

56
00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:57.720
Come build it with me.

57
00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.420
I'm Connor with Honor, over and out.

